<title>GERMANY: Siemens details H1 96/97 results by unit.</title>
<headline>Siemens details H1 96/97 results by unit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half results to</p>
<p>March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless noted).</p>
<p>Numbers in parentheses provide percentage change without the</p>
<p>effects of acquisitions</p>
<p>				    Orders   Change    Sales   Change</p>
<p>						 in pct		in pct</p>
<p>Energy</p>
<p>    Power Gen KWU	     4,000    -20	 2,400   -28</p>
<p>    Transmission		3,400    +15	 2,400    +6</p>
<p>Industry</p>
<p>    Building Systems ANL    4,600     -4	 4,100    +6</p>
<p>    Drives ASI		  4,400     +2	 4,100    +2</p>
<p>    Automation AUT	    3,300     -6	 2,900    -4</p>
<p>Communication</p>
<p>    Public Comms ON	   9,000    +52(+33)  6,300   +31(+23)</p>
<p>    Private Comms PN	  5,100    +28(+11)  4,900   +30(+11)</p>
<p>    Defense Electronics SI    600    -14	   600   -16</p>
<p>  Info Systems SNI	    7,600    +10	 7,200    +9</p>
<p>Transportation</p>
<p>    Transport Sys VT	  3,200    +46	 1,600   -11</p>
<p>    Automotive AT	     2,200    +15	 2,200   +15</p>
<p>  Medical Systems MED	 3,600     +3	 3,400    +1</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>    Semiconductors HL	 2,600     -8	 2,300    -2</p>
<p>    Passive Comp PR	   1,200     +4	 1,000    +1</p>
<p>    Electromechanical EC	600     -6	   600    -4</p>
<p>  Lighting/Osram		3,200     +9	 3,200    +9</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
